## Summary

I shipped a production-polished native Apple SwiftUI **`ExportModal`** at full parity with `features/dashboard/components/ExportModal.tsx`, following the established modals-dialogs architecture (proven by siblings `DashboardSettingsModal`/`ShareDriveDialog`).

**Deliverable** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/`, 11 files, ~2,500 lines):
- `Adapter` (value model + enums), `Projection` (pure logic), `Seams` (telemetry/clipboard/download/origin/date/source + i18n + a11y), `Model` (`@Observable` state holder), `States` (header/freshness/banners/loading/empty/error), `Views` (mini-grid, summary chips, download + copy rows, warning), entry `swift`, `Previews`, `strings`, plus `Tests` + `ModelTests`.

**Parity reproduced:** pretty JSON + byte-size badge (B/KB), minimal export → URL-safe base64 share link (`#import=`) with the >2000-char guard + warning, mini-grid geometry, download/copy-JSON/copy-URL actions, every state (loading/empty/error/populated + stale/offline), all web i18n keys, and VoiceOver labels on every interactive element.

